<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<title>Drone 4Ren report - case {{ meta.case_number }}</title>
<style>
  body { font-family: Georgia, 'Times New Roman', serif; margin: 2.5rem auto;
         max-width: 60rem; color: #1a1a1a; line-height: 1.45; }
  h1 { font-size: 1.6rem; border-bottom: 3px double #444; padding-bottom: .4rem; }
  h2 { font-size: 1.2rem; margin-top: 2.2rem; border-bottom: 1px solid #999;
       padding-bottom: .2rem; }
  table { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; font-size: .82rem; margin: .6rem 0; }
  th, td { border: 1px solid #bbb; padding: .28rem .5rem; text-align: left;
           vertical-align: top; }
  th { background: #f0f0ea; }
  code, .mono { font-family: Consolas, Menlo, monospace; font-size: .78rem;
                word-break: break-all; }
  .badge { display: inline-block; font-family: Consolas, monospace; font-size: .62rem;
           padding: .1rem .45rem; border-radius: 3px; vertical-align: middle;
           letter-spacing: .05em; }
  .src { background: #dfeadf; border: 1px solid #7a9a7a; }
  .der { background: #fdeeda; border: 1px solid #c09a5a; }
  .sev-alert { color: #8b0000; font-weight: bold; }
  .sev-warning { color: #8a6d00; font-weight: bold; }
  .sev-info { color: #33516e; }
  .note { font-size: .8rem; color: #555; font-style: italic; }
  .ok { color: #1c6b1c; font-weight: bold; }
  .fail { color: #8b0000; font-weight: bold; }
  svg { border: 1px solid #bbb; background: #fbfbf7; max-width: 100%; height: auto; }
  footer { margin-top: 3rem; font-size: .75rem; color: #666;
           border-top: 1px solid #999; padding-top: .5rem; }
  @media print { body { margin: 1cm; max-width: none; } }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<h1>UAS Flight Data Report</h1>
<table>
  <tr><th>Case number</th><td>{{ meta.case_number }}</td>
      <th>Case id</th><td class="mono">{{ meta.case_id }}</td></tr>
  <tr><th>Context</th><td>{{ meta.context }}</td>
      <th>Operator label</th><td>{{ meta.collector }}</td></tr>
  <tr><th>Case created (UTC)</th><td>{{ meta.created_utc }}</td>
      <th>Report generated (UTC)</th><td>{{ generated_utc }}</td></tr>
  <tr><th>Activity label</th><td>{{ actor }}</td>
      <th>Tool</th><td>droneforen {{ tool_version }} (Python {{ python_version }})</td></tr>
  {% if meta.description %}<tr><th>Description</th><td colspan="3">{{ meta.description }}</td></tr>{% endif %}
</table>
<p class="note">Sections are labeled
<span class="badge src">SOURCE-DERIVED</span> (read directly from evidence by a
versioned parser) or <span class="badge der">ANALYST-DERIVED</span> (computed from
source events by the stated method). Derived statements are working hypotheses,
not conclusions. This report's SHA-256 is written to a sidecar file at generation
time; verify it before relying on a printed or forwarded copy.</p>

<h2>1. Integrity verification at generation time</h2>
<p>
Evidence items rehashed: {{ verify.store.item_count }} -
{% if verify.store.ok %}<span class="ok">all hashes match</span>{% else %}<span class="fail">MISMATCHES FOUND</span>{% endif %}<br>
Audit log: {{ verify.audit.record_count }} records -
{% if verify.audit.ok %}<span class="ok">hash chain intact</span>{% else %}<span class="fail">CHAIN BROKEN</span>{% endif %}<br>
Audit chain head: <code>{{ verify.audit.head_sha256 }}</code>
</p>
{% if verify.problems %}
<table><tr><th>Integrity problem</th></tr>
{% for p in verify.problems %}<tr><td class="fail">{{ p }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}
</table>
{% endif %}

<h2>2. Evidence inventory <span class="badge src">SOURCE-DERIVED</span></h2>
<table>
<tr><th>Item</th><th>SHA-256</th><th>Size</th><th>Acquisition</th><th>Data origin</th>
<th>Added (UTC)</th><th>By</th></tr>
{% for ev in evidence %}
<tr><td>{{ ev.original_name }}{% if ev.description %}<br><span class="note">{{ ev.description }}</span>{% endif %}</td>
<td class="mono">{{ ev.sha256 }}</td><td>{{ ev.size_bytes }}</td>
<td>{{ ev.acquisition_method }}</td><td>{{ ev.data_origin }}</td>
<td>{{ ev.added_utc }}</td><td>{{ ev.actor }}</td></tr>
{% endfor %}
</table>

<h2>3. Flight reconstruction <span class="badge der">ANALYST-DERIVED</span></h2>
{% if flights %}
{% for f in flights %}
<h3 style="font-size:1rem">{{ f.evidence_name }} <span class="note">({{ f.evidence_sha256[:12] }}, parsed by {{ f.parser }})</span></h3>
<table>
<tr>
<th>First fix (UTC)</th><td>{{ f.first_fix_utc or "-" }}</td>
<th>Last fix (UTC)</th><td>{{ f.last_fix_utc or "-" }}</td></tr>
<tr><th>Track duration</th><td>{{ "%.1f s"|format(f.duration_s) if f.duration_s is not none else "-" }}</td>
<th>Path distance</th><td>{{ "%.0f m"|format(f.path_distance_m) if f.path_distance_m is not none else "-" }}</td></tr>
<tr><th>Max altitude</th><td>{% if f.max_alt_agl_m is not none %}{{ "%.1f m AGL"|format(f.max_alt_agl_m) }}{% elif f.max_alt_msl_m is not none %}{{ "%.1f m MSL"|format(f.max_alt_msl_m) }}{% else %}-{% endif %}</td>
<th>Max recorded speed</th><td>{{ "%.1f m/s"|format(f.max_speed_ms) if f.max_speed_ms is not none else "-" }}</td></tr>
<tr><th>Position fixes</th><td colspan="3">{{ f.position_count }} (after parser downsampling; original evidence retains full rate)</td></tr>
</table>
<table>
<tr><th>Derived item</th><th>Time (UTC)</th><th>Detail</th><th>Method</th></tr>
{% for item in f.items %}
<tr><td>{{ item.kind }}</td><td>{{ item.ts_utc or "-" }}</td>
<td>{{ item.description }}{% if item.lat is not none %}<br><span class="mono">{{ "%.6f"|format(item.lat) }}, {{ "%.6f"|format(item.lon) }}</span>{% endif %}</td>
<td class="note">{{ item.method }}</td></tr>
{% endfor %}
</table>
{% endfor %}
{% else %}<p class="note">No flight telemetry sources in this case.</p>{% endif %}

<h2>4. Track map <span class="badge der">ANALYST-DERIVED</span></h2>
{% if svg_map %}
{# generated by droneforen.report.make_track_svg, which escapes embedded names #}
{{ svg_map | safe }}
<p class="note">Local plot of parsed position fixes with no basemap. Use the exported
KML/GPX/GeoJSON for GIS overlay.</p>
{% else %}<p class="note">No positions to plot.</p>{% endif %}

<h2>5. Media correlation <span class="badge der">ANALYST-DERIVED</span></h2>
{% if correlations %}
<table>
<tr><th>Media</th><th>Capture (UTC)</th><th>Correlated</th><th>Track position at capture</th>
<th>EXIF vs track offset</th><th>Notes</th></tr>
{% for c in correlations %}
<tr><td>{{ c.media_name }}<br><span class="mono">{{ c.media_sha256[:12] }}</span></td>
<td>{{ c.ts_utc or "-" }}</td>
<td>{{ "yes" if c.correlated else "no" }}</td>
<td>{% if c.correlated %}<span class="mono">{{ "%.6f"|format(c.track_lat) }}, {{ "%.6f"|format(c.track_lon) }}</span>{% if c.track_alt_msl is not none %} @ {{ c.track_alt_msl }} m MSL{% endif %}<br><span class="note">from {{ c.track_evidence_name }}</span>{% else %}-{% endif %}</td>
<td>{% if c.offset_m is not none %}{{ c.offset_m }} m{% else %}-{% endif %}</td>
<td class="note">{{ c.reason or "" }}</td></tr>
{% endfor %}
</table>
{% else %}<p class="note">No media capture events in this case.</p>{% endif %}

<h2>6. Plausibility &amp; integrity findings <span class="badge der">ANALYST-DERIVED</span></h2>
{% if findings %}
<table>
<tr><th>Severity</th><th>Check</th><th>Description</th></tr>
{% for f in findings %}
<tr><td class="sev-{{ f.severity }}">{{ f.severity|upper }}</td>
<td>{{ f.check }}</td><td>{{ f.description }}</td></tr>
{% endfor %}
</table>
{% else %}<p class="note">No findings: all plausibility and integrity checks passed.
Absence of findings is not proof of authenticity.</p>{% endif %}

<h2>7. Unified timeline <span class="badge src">SOURCE-DERIVED</span></h2>
<p class="note">{{ timeline_summary.total_events }} events total
({{ timeline_summary.anchored_events }} UTC-anchored,
{{ timeline_summary.unanchored_events }} on unanchored clocks{% if timeline_truncated %};
showing the first {{ timeline_entries|length }} - full timeline via
<code>droneforen analyze timeline</code> or CSV export{% endif %}).</p>
<table>
<tr><th>Time (UTC)</th><th>Event</th><th>Position</th><th>Detail</th><th>Source</th></tr>
{% for e in timeline_entries %}
<tr><td>{{ e.ts_utc or ("(" ~ (e.ts_original or "no time") ~ " " ~ (e.clock_confidence or "") ~ ")") }}</td>
<td>{{ e.event_type }}</td>
<td>{% if e.lat is not none %}<span class="mono">{{ "%.6f"|format(e.lat) }}, {{ "%.6f"|format(e.lon) }}</span>{% if e.alt_agl is not none %} {{ "%.0f"|format(e.alt_agl) }}m AGL{% elif e.alt_msl is not none %} {{ "%.0f"|format(e.alt_msl) }}m MSL{% endif %}{% endif %}</td>
<td class="mono">{{ e.payload_compact }}</td>
<td class="note">{{ e.evidence_name }} · {{ e.source_offset or "" }} · {{ e.parser_name }} {{ e.parser_version }}</td></tr>
{% endfor %}
</table>

<h2>8. Reproducibility appendix</h2>
<h3 style="font-size:1rem">Parser runs</h3>
<table>
<tr><th>Run id</th><th>Evidence (input SHA-256)</th><th>Parser</th><th>Status</th>
<th>Events</th><th>Started (UTC)</th><th>Ended (UTC)</th><th>Settings</th></tr>
{% for r in parser_runs %}
<tr><td class="mono">{{ r.id }}</td><td class="mono">{{ r.input_sha256 }}</td>
<td>{{ r.parser_name }} {{ r.parser_version }}</td><td>{{ r.status }}</td>
<td>{{ r.event_count if r.event_count is not none else "-" }}</td>
<td>{{ r.started_utc }}</td><td>{{ r.ended_utc or "-" }}</td>
<td class="mono">{{ r.settings_json }}</td></tr>
{% endfor %}
</table>
<p class="note">To reproduce: intake the evidence files listed in section 2 (verify
SHA-256), run each parser at the listed version over the corresponding item, and
compare event output. The case database is derived and can be rebuilt from
evidence plus these runs. MD5 values are recorded in evidence manifests for legacy
inventory interoperability only.</p>

<footer>
Generated by droneforen {{ tool_version }} on {{ generated_utc }} by {{ actor }}.
Audit chain head at generation: <code>{{ verify.audit.head_sha256 }}</code> ·
Report SHA-256 in adjacent <code>.sha256</code> sidecar file.
</footer>
</body>
</html>
